{"version":1,"made_by":"Brush, 2026-10-30","ken":"make spells an event: bigger, slower, magical, earth-shattering, completely serious but absolutely ridiculous","files":"art/spell-fx/<spell>/<spell>-<layer>.webp = PC / full-resolution version (about 450-600 px, the painted original); <spell>-<layer>-m.webp = phone version (max 320 px). Load the -m files on phones (small screen or touch), the full ones on PC. Layers: core, glow, particles, ring, debris, word","platform":"PC first (Ken, Oct 30: mostly played on PC, serious players on PC), still reads and runs well on phones","conventions":{"scale":"sizes are in board squares (1 = one square wide); the layer keeps its own aspect ratio","blend":"glow, ring and particles draw with additive blending (canvas \"lighter\" / THREE.AdditiveBlending); core, debris and word draw normally","ring":"the ring art is already drawn at a slight top-down angle; lay it flat on the board under the target","word":"the sound-word starburst always faces the camera, pops in with an overshoot (0 -> 1.25 -> 1.0 over 220 ms), wobbles +/-6 deg, holds, then fades; keep it on screen at least 600 ms so phones can read it","shake":"0..1, light: 1 = 6 px camera shake for 250 ms at impact; never more than that (tutorial and card text must stay readable)","slowmo":"true = the game runs at 0.35x speed for 300 ms right at impact (only the FX and units, not the timers)","flash":"a full-screen flash of the tint colour at impact, 0.18 opacity, 120 ms (skip if shake is 0)","easing":"outBack for pops, inQuad for falls, outCubic for travel, linear fades"},"spells":{"fireball":{"name":"Searing Arcane Orb","target":"unit_or_commander","path":"arc","path_notes":"core flies from the caster (Commander or played card) to the target on a high arc, spinning slowly, glow trailing behind it","total_ms":2200,"tint":"#ff7a1a","sound_word":"FWOOSH!","shake":0.35,"slowmo":true,"layers":{"core":{"file":"art/spell-fx/fireball/fireball-core.webp","px":[506,521],"file_phone":"ar